# Development

Use a configured package registry when available. A local alpha smoke test can instead use wheels
built from the OpenSDL framework checkout:

```bash
uv sync --find-links /path/to/OpenSDL/dist
./scripts/check.sh
./scripts/dev.sh
```

Because the wheelhouse location can be recorded in `uv.lock`, use a stable registry or committed
artifact source before treating the lockfile as portable. Set the repository variable
`OPENSDL_PACKAGES_AVAILABLE=true` only after CI can resolve that source.

Add organization-specific behavior under `src/{{ package }}/`. Install public
or private adapters through normal Python dependencies and declare them in
`opensdl.yaml`. Every physical adapter should have a simulator and a deployment-
controlled hardware test plan.
